{
  "description": "Numerical building blocks. A composite Simpson's rule approximates a definite integral over [a,b] using a number of sub-intervals that MUST be even; when the interval count is odd the routine emits the notice line \"The composite simpson's rule needs even intervals!\" and yields no value. The lower incomplete gamma function, the beta function (which is exactly 1 when both parameters are 1) and the regularized incomplete beta function are also exposed. For the named integrands, \"square\" integrates x^2 and \"sine\" integrates sin(x); the Simpson result is reported floored to the nearest lower integer.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.simpson_rule",
        "args": {
          "a": 0,
          "b": 3,
          "intervals": 1000,
          "function": "square"
        }
      },
      "expected_output": "9\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.simpson_rule",
        "args": {
          "a": 0,
          "b": 2,
          "intervals": 100,
          "function": "identity"
        }
      },
      "expected_output": "2\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.simpson_rule",
        "args": {
          "a": 0,
          "b": 10,
          "intervals": 4,
          "function": "identity"
        }
      },
      "expected_output": "58\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.simpson_rule",
        "args": {
          "a": 0,
          "b": 3.141592653589793,
          "intervals": 1000,
          "function": "sine"
        }
      },
      "expected_output": "2\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.simpson_rule",
        "args": {
          "a": 1,
          "b": 5,
          "intervals": 7,
          "function": "square"
        }
      },
      "expected_output": "The composite simpson's rule needs even intervals!\nnil\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.simpson_rule",
        "args": {
          "a": 0,
          "b": 4,
          "intervals": 2,
          "function": "square"
        }
      },
      "expected_output": "26\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.lower_incomplete_gamma",
        "args": {
          "s": 1,
          "x": 2
        },
        "round": 6
      },
      "expected_output": "0.864703\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.lower_incomplete_gamma",
        "args": {
          "s": 2,
          "x": 5
        },
        "round": 6
      },
      "expected_output": "0.959573\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.beta",
        "args": {
          "x": 1,
          "y": 2
        },
        "round": 6
      },
      "expected_output": "0.5\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.beta",
        "args": {
          "x": 2,
          "y": 1
        },
        "round": 6
      },
      "expected_output": "0.5\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.beta",
        "args": {
          "x": 6,
          "y": 2
        },
        "round": 6
      },
      "expected_output": "0.02381\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.incomplete_beta",
        "args": {
          "x": 0.0,
          "alpha": 2,
          "beta": 2
        },
        "round": 6
      },
      "expected_output": "0.0\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.incomplete_beta",
        "args": {
          "x": 0.5,
          "alpha": 2,
          "beta": 2
        },
        "round": 6
      },
      "expected_output": "0.5\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "op": "math.incomplete_beta",
        "args": {
          "x": 0.3,
          "alpha": 1,
          "beta": 1
        },
        "round": 6
      },
      "expected_output": "0.3\n"
    }
  ]
}
